[E0440] Error: `texture` is `G::Texture`, which cannot be cloned
    ╭─[ err/572_derived_field_of_decided_type/main.wip:12:2 ]
    │
 10 │ @derive(Clone)
    │         ──┬──
    │           ╰──── `@derive(Clone)` writes the clone field by field
    │
 12 │     texture: G::Texture
    │     ─────────┬─────────
    │              ╰─────────── not a field that clones
    │
    │ Help: what `@derive` writes asks its conditions of the type's parameters, and `G::Texture` is decided by one; write the implementation by hand, or take it as a parameter of the type's own, which a condition can name
    │
    │ Note: a field clones when its type implements `Clone`: plain data, which owns no memory, is its own clone, and so are a `String`, a `Vec`, an `Option` or a tuple of what clones, and a type that asks for `@derive(Clone)` or writes `extend …: Clone`
────╯
